-- title:
--   Non-zero primes are maximal in rings between k and F
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $F$ be a field carrying an $A$-algebra structure, and let $t \in F$ be such that $F$ is algebraic over the $A$-subalgebra $A[t] =$ `Algebra.adjoin A {t}` generated by the image of $A$ together with $t$ (so that, over the fraction field of the image of $A$, the field $F$ has transcendence degree at most one). Let $S$ be an $A$-subalgebra of $F$ with the property that for every $a : A$ whose image $\operatorname{algebraMap} A F\,a$ in $F$ is non-zero, the inverse $(\operatorname{algebraMap} A F\,a)^{-1}$ lies in $S$; since $S$ contains the image of $A$ itself, this says that $S$ contains the field of fractions of that image. Let $P$ be a prime ideal of $S$ (the hypothesis `P.IsPrime` being an instance argument) with $P \neq \bot$. The conclusion is that $P$ is a maximal ideal of $S$. Note that $t$ enters only through the algebraicity hypothesis, and that no Noetherian or finiteness condition is imposed on $S$.
--
--   This is the statement that a ring $S$ sandwiched between the constant field and a field $F$ of transcendence degree at most one has Krull dimension at most one, i.e. the relevant case of the dimension inequality $\operatorname{ht} P + \operatorname{tr.deg} \kappa(P) \le \operatorname{tr.deg} S$. It is used in the local study of points of curves, feeding the characterisation of local rings of a universally closed integrally closed scheme as valuation subrings and the description of which valuation subrings contain a given prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subalgebra_isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot_of_isAlgebraic_adjoin_singleton.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
